      "math_academy_id": "q-90669",
      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-5,4],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-5$ and $b=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(4-(-5))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{81}{12}=\\frac{27}{4}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{27}{4}}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}≈2.598.\n$$",
